# Contributions

Crosstalk is planned to be quite a large project and I have decided to allow contributions to be submitted.
They will function in a way similar to the kernel DCO process. I like it because I recently stopped using git
and don't want to walk that back, so instead, to contribute, just send me your patch by email at **dangling@danglingptr.io**
I might not accept patches that are not compatible with the ecosystem that I want to build. However, if you submit something
really cool, I will definitely consider it. And as far as bugfixes go, I will always consider but may not always apply them
for a variety of reasons. Make sure that the content that you submit is yours, that you're sending it under
the **GNU AGPLv3-only**, and that it is **signed-off by you**. If you'd like to sign your patch, then you are welcome
to enclose it using PGP, and I will then associate your sign-off identifier with your pubkey. Thanks

My key's fingerprint: 5FEDF7367C81E61DC2EA604AEBE6B5D5B3373C15


Patch format:

```
<patch description>

Signed-off-by: [Name|Stable identifier] <yourname.orstableidentifier@youremailserver.org>
---
<patch in a unified diff against a release>
```


DCO verbatim (https://developercertificate.org/):

> Developer Certificate of Origin
